{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>There shall not be to you.</b> Do not say: I will serve you and them — for I alone took you out; and further, you have no need of them, for they are vanity and emptiness; they cannot help." "<b>Elohim others.</b> That others call them Elohim. Why are they called by the name Elohim? Rabbi Yosi says: so that there be no opening to say, they were not called Elohim — for had they been called Elohim, they would have had validity." "<b>Others.</b> Rabbi Eliezer says: because they are other (different) every day — if it was of gold and was needed, he makes it of silver; of silver, he makes it of bronze; of bronze, he makes it of iron; of iron, he makes it of wood. Therefore they are called Elohim others." "<b>There shall not be to you Elohim others.</b> The dominion of others." "<b>Upon My face.</b> That is: you shall not have another master in My place. A parallel: על פני בן השנואה הבכור; וכהן אלעזר על פני אהרן. Another interpretation: if you accept him upon yourself as master, know that he will be על פני ועל אפי. A parallel: חמס ושוד ישמע בה על פני; אם לא אל פניך יברכך."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:58.356570872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}